WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.869
-Good evening, I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:03.870
We hope you're doing well,
and now, if you don't mind,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.271
we're gonna get to the news.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:08.274
According to estimates from
the Congressional Budget Office,

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:11.644
President Biden's plan to
forgive $10,000 per borrower

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:15.281
in Federal Student loan debt
will cost nearly $400 billion.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:18.784
Or, in student loan terms,
$27 a month

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:20.453
for 30 billion years.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.722
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.891
According to new data,
coronavirus cases

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:27.460
are rising in the U.K.,
maybe because last week,

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.563
the entire country
attended the same event.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:33.399
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:35.768
The White House announced
yesterday that President Biden

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:37.036
will host French President

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.904
Emmanuel Macron
later this year.

00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:41.908
Which is great, but can we say
no gifts this time?

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.510
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.077
[ French accent ] "We noticed
you did not have

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:47.714
a 305-foot woman, and..."

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.548
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.548 --> 00:00:52.552
"New York famously
has much space, oui?"

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.254
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.523 --> 00:00:59.592
[ Normal voice ] That's -- so,
in 2022,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:03.796
one of our monologue writers
were like, "Enough.

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:06.065
I'm going after
the Statue of Liberty."

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.866
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.866 --> 00:01:10.336
Republican Congressman
Matt Gaetz announced last week

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:11.838
that he is starting
his own Twitch

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:15.007
streaming channel, and tweeted,
"I'm joining Twitch to bring

00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:18.311
my America-first message to a
new generation of voters."

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.446
Previously, the only way
he reached a new generation

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.081
of voters was on Venmo.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:24.317
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:28.154
Scientists recently discovered
vaccine-resistant coronavirus

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:29.321
in Russian bats.

00:01:29.321 --> 00:01:31.591
It's what Putin's calling
Plan B.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:34.293
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:35.395
"Release the bats."

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:37.629
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.629 --> 00:01:40.600
A panel of doctors recommended
last week that all adults

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.635
under 65-years-old

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.503
should be regularly screened
for anxiety.

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:46.705
Said adults, "How regularly?
Like, once a year?

00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:48.474
Once a month?
Every day?

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:49.875
Should we screen every day?

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:51.611
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:54.948
"Rolling Stone" yesterday
published an updated

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:57.684
list of the 100 greatest
TV shows of all-time.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:02:01.654
And I don't want to brag,
but I read the whole list.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.889
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.889 --> 00:02:06.359
Not bad, not bad.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.860
100, read 'em all.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.595
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:12.332
According to a new survey,
24% of Americans said

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:15.068
that they found it very easy
to make friends as a teenager,

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.904
and the other 76%
are the people they bullied.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.272
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.272 --> 00:02:22.575
A woman in North Dakota
was arrested recently

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:26.746
after she allegedly brought
a wild raccoon into a bar.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:30.116
Said the woman, "Oh, I thought
you said it was rabies night."

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.218
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:36.989
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:39.725
So, the premise of Brian --
I'll say his name --

00:02:39.725 --> 00:02:41.427
the premise of Brian's joke...

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.463
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:46.632
...is that you would hear a bar
was having "ladies night"

00:02:46.632 --> 00:02:48.468
and you would hear it
as "rabies night."

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:51.404
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.640
Maybe that's a symptom
that you have rabies.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.442
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:59.178
You're home
with your pet raccoon,

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:01.113
and it bites you, and then,
like, an hour later,

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:02.415
you're like,
"Did I hear rabies night?"

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:05.351
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:08.587
And finally --
we just let 'em all in, guys.

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:10.055
We're just finding out with you

00:03:10.055 --> 00:03:11.491
if they're good or not,
you know?

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:14.093
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:16.095
And finally, according
to a new survey,

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:19.098
78% of animal owners said
that seeing their pet

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.966
when they come home is the best
part of their day.

00:03:20.966 --> 00:03:23.169
Worst part of their day,
when their spouse

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:24.303
heard them say that.

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:26.005
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:28.241
And that was the monologue,
everybody.

